   "evidence": "Pullback.lean:259-265 (`rw [chartTerm_apply, chartTerm_apply, h\u03c7s, ...]` \u2026 `erw [h]`) and the new lines `rw [chartTermExtend_apply, chartTermExtend_apply, h\u03c7s, ...]` \u2026 `erw [h]`. Chart.lean:87-90 and 248-252 show that `chartTerm` and `chartTermExtend` differ only in the first component of the `tangentHom` base point and in the vector.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Symplectic/Manifold/AlmostComplex/Inhomogeneous/Pullback.lean",
   "fix": "Add one pointwise lemma for an arbitrary base point `x : P` and vector `w`: `2 \u2022 mvfderiv I \u03c7 (\u03c7.symm v) ((\u03bd.pullback g hnr).val.tangentHom (x, \u03c7.symm v) w) = 2 \u2022 mvfderiv I' \u03c8 (\u03c8.symm v) (\u03bd.val.tangentHom (x, \u03c8.symm v) w)`, given `h\u03c7` and `h\u03c7s`. Make the projection explicit there, e.g. with `Prod.snd` simp or `dsimp only at h` instead of `erw`. Then prove `chartTerm_pullback` and `chartTermExtend_pullback` as `funext` plus `chartTerm_apply`/`chartTermExtend_apply` and that lemma.",
   "issue": "`chartTermExtend_pullback` copies the proof of `chartTerm_pullback` (lines 254-265) line for line: same `set y`/`hy`, the same `rw` chain through `mvfderiv_apply_eq_mfderiv_apply` and `g.mfderiv_comp_diffeomorph`, and the same `erw [h]` that relies on the projection `(q, y).2` reducing to `y`. The two proofs differ only in the base point and the domain vector given to `tangentHom`. So the `erw` workaround now exists twice, and the reusable fact behind both proofs stays hidden.",
   "line": 290
  }
